    "created_at": "2021-04-16T08:37:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-16T08:37:36Z",
    "body": "I've sent https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/972 to define just the `XSLTProcessor` interface, pointing back to this issue.\r\n\r\nI went ahead and queried HTTP Archive for \"new XSLTProcessor\" to see what current usage looks like, and put the results in https://gist.github.com/foolip/d59bd1ab27b2c93a1a37b434074ea410.\r\n\r\nIt's \"only\" 7-8k sites, but my sense is that this is going to be found in more \"enterprise-y\" sites and that it's stuff nobody is around to maintain any longer. https://affiliates.skrill.com/includes/scripts/xmlxsl.js is a good example, where if that code is actually used (not checked) all modern browsers would go down the `TransformXML_Moz` path and break at the `new XSLTProcessor()` call.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
